    "code_context": "from difflow import IdealThermo, get_species_data, mass_action_kinetics\n\nspecies = ['acetic_acid', 'ethanol', 'ethyl_acetate', 'water']\nthermo = IdealThermo({n: get_species_data(n) for n in species})\n\n# Fischer esterification: acetic acid + ethanol <=> ethyl acetate + water.\n# Reversible and equilibrium-limited. K_eq = 4 is the classic textbook\n# value for this system, and it caps a 1:1 feed at two-thirds conversion.\n# The forward Arrhenius constants are illustrative -- an acid-catalysed\n# rate of the right order, Ea = 60 kJ/mol -- not a fit to one catalyst.\nkin = mass_action_kinetics([{\n    'equation': 'acetic_acid + ethanol <=> ethyl_acetate + water',\n    'reactants': {'acetic_acid': 1.0, 'ethanol': 1.0},\n    'products': {'ethyl_acetate': 1.0, 'water': 1.0},\n    'reversible': True, 'K_eq': 4.0,\n    'rate_params': {'A': 18.0, 'Ea': 60_000.0, 'n': 0.0}}],\n    species, reverse='equilibrium')\n\n# The flash uses Raoult's law, which knows nothing of the ethyl acetate /\n# ethanol / water azeotropes: read its split as qualitative.\n",
    "title": "Esterification with recycle",
